{"id":8146,"date":"2021-10-15T10:14:35","date_gmt":"2021-10-15T14:14:35","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/?p=8146"},"modified":"2021-10-18T10:52:47","modified_gmt":"2021-10-18T14:52:47","slug":"tourist-review-dead-horse-point-state-park-se-utah","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/2021\/10\/15\/tourist-review-dead-horse-point-state-park-se-utah\/","title":{"rendered":"Tourist Review &#8211; Dead Horse Point State Park &#8211; SE Utah"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p>When we stayed a couple weeks at Angostura Recreation Area (Hot Springs SD) you&#8217;ll remember that we had the pleasure of meeting and visiting with our neighbors Clark &amp; Anita.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/10\/IMG_20211001_121533796.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"720\" height=\"540\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/10\/IMG_20211001_121533796.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-8149\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/10\/IMG_20211001_121533796.jpg 720w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/10\/IMG_20211001_121533796-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/10\/IMG_20211001_121533796-685x514.jpg 685w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 720px) 100vw, 720px\" \/><\/a><figcaption>Clark and Anita (and their Oliver Travel Trailer)<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>They told us that as we traveled south from South Dakota through Wyoming and Utah, we just HAD to stop (and camp if we could) at Dead Horse Point State Park just northwest of Moab, Utah.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>He told us if we didn&#8217;t make it to any of the other popular parks in that area of Utah (Arches, Canyonlands, Canyon de Chelly, Grand Staircase Escalante, Capital Reef) we&#8217;d just HAVE to visit Dead Horse.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>As it turned out, our travels back to Rover&#8217;s Roost at Casa Grande Arizona found us traveling west along southern Wyoming and the east side of Utah and traveling down U.S. 191 instead of using the interstate highway system &#8211; and we&#8217;re so glad we did!<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full is-resized\"><a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/10\/HS-to-Bluff-Map.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/10\/HS-to-Bluff-Map.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-8152\" width=\"714\" height=\"714\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/10\/HS-to-Bluff-Map.jpg 540w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/10\/HS-to-Bluff-Map-300x300.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/10\/HS-to-Bluff-Map-150x150.jpg 150w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/10\/HS-to-Bluff-Map-100x100.jpg 100w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 714px) 100vw, 714px\" \/><\/a><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>This way we stayed out of Colorado and the I-25 \/ I-70 yet we still got to see a LOT of beautiful scenery and ecosystems as we traveled up and down the hills and valleys, sometimes as high as 9000 feet!<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>But the Creme de la creme &#8211; has been Dead Horse Point State Park.  The Colorado River runs through the park.  The main (only) paved road through the park is Utah State Route 313 and it&#8217;s one way in and the same one way out.  The $20 (non-resident) entrance fee is per vehicle so we parked our rigs in a gravel parking area just outside the park entrance and then we climbed into David and Susan&#8217;s car to visit the park.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>As we all realize, photographs just never represent fully the depth and beauty of the subject.  But I just had to share some with you here.  <\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>If you click on any of the thumbnails below, a larger picture will open.  If you have a slower internet connection it might take a second (or a few) to sharpen up the image.  Just be patient and you should be able to see and appreciate the beauty in the detail.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped wp-block-gallery-1 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex\"><ul class=\"blocks-gallery-grid\"><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/10\/20211014110922.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"720\" height=\"540\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/10\/20211014110922.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"8154\" class=\"wp-image-8154\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/10\/20211014110922.jpg 720w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/10\/20211014110922-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/10\/20211014110922-685x514.jpg 685w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 720px) 100vw, 720px\" \/><\/a><\/figure><\/li><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/10\/20211014110039.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"720\" height=\"540\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/10\/20211014110039.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"8155\" class=\"wp-image-8155\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/10\/20211014110039.jpg 720w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/10\/20211014110039-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/10\/20211014110039-685x514.jpg 685w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 720px) 100vw, 720px\" \/><\/a><\/figure><\/li><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/10\/IMG_20211014_101008678_HDR.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"720\" height=\"540\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/10\/IMG_20211014_101008678_HDR.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"8156\" class=\"wp-image-8156\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/u